t condition:** INDEPENDENT\n**Automated operational score:** 85/100 — LOW — APPROVE\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **MEDIUM · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · Inbound HTTP (port 80) permitted in cleartext instead of HTTPS**\n  - Category rationale: The NSG explicitly allows inbound TCP port 80 (plaintext HTTP) from an approved source. Port 80 transmits credentials, tokens, and data without encryption. This is a concrete, demonstrable weakness in the supplied code regardless of whether the workload is research or production.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_network_security_group.nsg, security_rule 'AllowHTTP': priority=302, direction=Inbound, access=Allow, protocol=Tcp, destination_port_range=80, source_address_prefix=203.0.113.10/32.\n  - Analysis: The AllowHTTP security rule in azurerm_network_security_group.nsg permits inbound TCP traffic on port 80 from 203.0.113.10/32. Port 80 is unencrypted HTTP; any communication over this rule is susceptible to interception and man-in-the-middle attacks on the network path between the test harness and the subnet. Even for a research workload, allowing plaintext HTTP as the permitted protocol introduces unnecessary risk. If the test harness communicates over HTTP, credentials, tokens, or research data may be exposed in transit.\n  - Impact: Traffic between the approved test-harness host and resources in the subnet transits in plaintext. An attacker with access to the network path (e.g., within the VNet or on the path from 203.0.113.10) could intercept or modify HTTP payloads, including any authentication material or research data exchanged over port 80.\n  - Recommendation: Replace destination_port_range=80 with destination_port_range=443 (HTTPS) and ensure the test harness communicates over TLS. If both ports are genuinely required, add a justified comment and scope port 80 to the minimum necessary duration. Do not allow port 80 as a permanent inbound rule without documented justification.\n\n### Policy mappings\n- **SEC-001** — No resource should be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified. (finding F-001)\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6147857808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"GitHub Actions","description":"Automate your workflow from idea to production","external_url":"https://help.github.com/en/actions","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","created_at":"2018-07-30T09:30:17Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T16:17:48Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","artifact_metadata":"write","attestations":"write","checks":"write","code_quality":"write","contents":"write","copi